WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:01.768
[music playing]

00:00:01.835 --> 00:00:03.570
ALBERT LIN: It's literally
a city in the clouds.

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:05.271
Maybe those Spanish
stories weren't

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:09.175
just legends because that's what
a real lost city looks like.

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:10.744
HELICOPTER PILOT:
[inaudible] 1 0 1 2.

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:13.713
ALBERT LIN: That's Ciudad
Perdida, the Lost City.

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:19.753
Ciudad Perdida, the
Lost City, is high

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:23.022
up in Colombia's most
isolated mountain range,

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:23.823
the Sierra Nevada.

00:00:28.628 --> 00:00:30.530
Archaeologists
have spent decades

00:00:30.597 --> 00:00:33.500
exploring this dense jungle to
find out about the people who

00:00:33.566 --> 00:00:38.371
lived here over 500 years ago.

00:00:38.438 --> 00:00:44.577
Digital technology will help
them reveal more and faster.

00:00:44.644 --> 00:00:47.714
[chuckles]

00:00:51.284 --> 00:00:53.319
Only the world's
toughest archaeologists

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:55.088
can handle this terrain.

00:00:55.155 --> 00:00:59.526
Santiago Giraldo has been
excavating here for 20 years.

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:03.463
[chuckles] It's a
beautiful place.

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:05.665
[helicopter]

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:08.101
It's amazing this place
is still standing.

00:01:08.168 --> 00:01:09.469
Who discovered it?

00:01:09.536 --> 00:01:11.571
SANTIAGO GIRALDO: It was
like [spanish],, looters.

00:01:11.638 --> 00:01:13.440
And then the
archaeologists came in.

00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:15.375
Took them about a
week to get here.

00:01:15.442 --> 00:01:18.777
And they were led
by other looters.

00:01:18.845 --> 00:01:20.313
Looters led the way, huh?

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:22.782
Yeah, it's actually pretty
incredible because they were--

00:01:22.849 --> 00:01:24.317
they got into a shotgun fight.

00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:28.521
The looters were after the
gold that's in the burials.

00:01:28.588 --> 00:01:32.658
And one looter came out with,
you know, more than 80 pieces

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:33.726
of gold from one burial.

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:34.561
Wow.

00:01:34.627 --> 00:01:36.329
Yeah.

00:01:36.396 --> 00:01:38.731
ALBERT LIN: Gunfights for gold.

00:01:38.798 --> 00:01:41.534
Archeology gets dangerous
when gold is involved.

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:44.637
And this place is
bursting with it.

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:45.738
Who built all this?

00:01:45.805 --> 00:01:47.907
It was a people that
we call the Tayrona.

00:01:47.974 --> 00:01:49.776
Their predecessors,
the [inaudible]

00:01:49.843 --> 00:01:51.144
built it around 600 AD.

00:01:54.147 --> 00:01:55.215
It's huge.

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:58.718
[music playing]

00:02:08.026 --> 00:02:09.262
How many people
would've lived here?

00:02:09.329 --> 00:02:12.298
About 2,000 to
3,000 at its peak.

00:02:12.365 --> 00:02:14.267
And then about
10,000 people living

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:15.468
in the upper part of the basin.

00:02:15.535 --> 00:02:16.135
10,000?

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:17.670
Yeah.

00:02:17.737 --> 00:02:19.372
All that forest that you see
would have been all farmland.

00:02:27.113 --> 00:02:30.583
Aw, man, you can almost feel
their energy here, you know?

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:31.918
Like all these people
running around.

00:02:39.726 --> 00:02:42.428
SANTIAGO GIRALDO: It's taken
us over 40 years of work

00:02:42.495 --> 00:02:46.065
to clear out and
survey the site, trying

00:02:46.132 --> 00:02:48.201
to tease out what these
people were thinking

00:02:48.268 --> 00:02:50.336
when they were building it.

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:51.170
ALBERT LIN: 40 years?

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:52.772
SANTIAGO GIRALDO: Yep.

